{
  "name": "Chat with your Google Drive documents using past.dev memory and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## A knowledge chatbot on your Google Drive, with no vector store\n\nFor teams that want to ask questions about their documents and get the current answer, with the date and the document it comes from.\n\n### How it works\n- When a file is created or updated in one Drive folder, n8n downloads it and extracts the text.\n- A Code node splits long documents at paragraph boundaries. Each part goes into past.dev with the file ID as its Source ID, so an updated file replaces its older version.\n- In the chat, the AI Agent calls past.dev **Recall** as a tool and answers from the documents. Simple Memory keeps the flow of the chat.\n\n### Setup\n1. Self-hosted n8n: open **Settings > Community Nodes**, select **Install** and enter `n8n-nodes-pastdotdev` (tested with 0.1.0 on n8n 2.47). [Installation guide](https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/community-nodes/installation/)\n2. Create a project API key in the [past.dev console](https://app.past.dev) and add it as a **Past Dev API** credential in each past.dev node.\n3. Add your Google Drive and OpenAI credentials.\n4. In both Drive triggers, choose the folder to watch.\n5. In **Config**, set `reader_identity`: the person or team the chat answers for.\n\n### Customization\n- No embeddings, chunks or vector database to manage: past.dev keeps what is true today and the history behind it.\n- Set an Audience in **Save the document part to memory** for confidential folders.\n- Supported here: Google Docs, text, Markdown and PDF files.\n",
        "height": 800,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "c11abc5b-e90b-5637-9229-62675c14a161",
      "name": "Sticky Note Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
